W=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P=Path('/workspace/shared/downloads');K='TRGD_ABCD_uniform_fonts'
cn_caption='''图X｜Temporal Root Graph Decoding（TRGD，V90）两类根时序分类的性能比较、整体流程消融及可视化结果。（A）归档评估中V66 U-Net与TRGD的Precision、Recall、Dice和IoU；橙色和蓝色分别表示新生根与既有根，虚线空心圆和实线方块分别表示两种模型。（B）固定最新版V35根系前景后，整套TRGD关闭与开启条件下的新生根、既有根及Macro Dice对比。（C）相同消融条件下新生根各项指标的变化；空心圆和蓝色方块分别表示TRGD off和TRGD on，Δ表示百分点差。（D）同一局部视野在T1—T4的原始RGB、人工参考标记、V66 U-Net及TRGD预测；橙色为新生根，蓝色为既有根，T1白色标记表示基准根系。比例尺为100像素。TRGD将ConvLSTM＋GAT预测、Axis根轴约束和Junction交叉连接约束作为整体执行。Macro Dice为两类根Dice的算术平均。'''
cn_note='''评估口径：A、D沿用归档比较配置；B、C使用新版V35第91轮前景及现有TRGD迁移部署接口，属于冻结权重下的整套推理消融。两套结果的前景配置不同，Macro Dice 90.95%→93.59%与89.14%→92.31%分别报告。定量指标均基于0353-2-B3开发序列T2—T4的468203个参考根系像素，背景不参与时序类别计分；T1仅提供基准。B、C两组同样保留17438个V35漏检参考根像素。该图未提供独立时序测试或重复训练的统计推断。'''
cn_sections=[('A｜归档模型比较','''TRGD的新生根Precision由86.71%升至94.51%，Recall由83.14%升至84.50%，Dice由84.88%升至89.23%，IoU由73.74%升至80.55%。新生根Dice提升4.34个百分点，较大的Precision增益表明参考根系像素中“既有根误分为新生根”的问题得到缓解。既有根Dice由97.02%升至97.96%，两类Macro Dice由90.95%升至93.59%，增加2.64个百分点。该比较反映归档配置下两种模型的汇总表现。'''),('B｜整套流程消融','''固定相同RGB、V35根系前景及冻结权重，开启整套TRGD后，新生根Dice由83.01%升至88.07%（+5.07个百分点），既有根Dice由95.28%升至96.55%（+1.27个百分点），Macro Dice由89.14%升至92.31%（+3.17个百分点）。收益主要集中于新生根状态判别。两组的前景差异为0，漏检参考根像素数均为17438，因此改善来自固定前景内的时序状态重新分配。本实验评估整套流程的联合贡献，不能据此分别量化ConvLSTM、GAT、Axis或Junction的独立贡献。'''),('C｜新生根性能权衡','''新生根Precision从82.01%提高至93.18%（+11.17个百分点），Recall从84.02%降至83.50%（−0.53个百分点）；Dice和IoU分别提高5.07和7.74个百分点。参考既有根被误分为新生根的像素由14517降至4812，而正确识别的新生根像素由66193略降至65778。这说明TRGD的新生根输出趋于保守，以减少错误新生标签换取少量检出损失；总体重叠指标仍改善。背景不在本次时序计分域内，因此这些Precision变化不应解释为根系/背景分割能力的变化。'''),('D｜时空对应与可视化解释','''D展示同一420×320像素局部窗口在四个时期的对应关系。T1以白色根系标记建立基准；T2可见较多橙色新生根段；T3和T4的蓝色既有根占比较高，同时仍可见少量橙色根段。并列的人工参考与模型列便于观察同一根段在交叉部位、细根分支和相邻时期中的状态分配。对该展示窗口的参考根像素进一步计数，T2错分由1701降至130，T4由135降至58，而T3由512升至693，表明局部改善并非逐期一致。该面板沿用归档配置，用于解释A中的定量比较；局部示例不代替全视野统计，也不据此宣称TRGD提高了上游二值根系检出率。'''),('结果解释范围','''A/D与B/C对应不同前景配置，93.59%与92.31%的差异不能直接解释为模型退化或额外增益。B/C为T2—T4汇总结果，并不表示逐期均有改善：其逐期明细显示T4新生根Dice从75.13%降至69.46%。因此结论应限定为该开发序列的总体时序分类改善，并保留后期新根识别的局限。单个序列中的大量相关像素不能作为独立生物学重复；本图不提供统计显著性结论。''')]
en_caption='''Figure X. Two-class temporal root classification, whole-pipeline ablation and qualitative comparison of Temporal Root Graph Decoding (TRGD, V90). (A) Precision, recall, Dice and intersection over union (IoU) for V66 U-Net and TRGD in the archived comparison. Gold and blue denote new and existing roots, respectively; dashed lines with open circles and solid lines with squares denote the two models. (B) New-root Dice, existing-root Dice and their unweighted mean (Macro Dice) with the complete TRGD process disabled or enabled on the latest fixed V35 foreground. (C) Corresponding changes in new-root precision, recall, Dice and IoU. Open circles and blue squares denote TRGD off and TRGD on; Δ is the difference in percentage points. (D) Original RGB, human reference, V66 U-Net and TRGD predictions for the same local field at T1–T4. Gold indicates new roots, blue indicates existing roots and white indicates the T1 root baseline. Scale bar: 100 pixels. ConvLSTM+GAT prediction, Axis root-axis constraints and Junction connection constraints are applied as one coupled TRGD process.'''
en_note='''Evaluation scope. A and D retain the archived configuration, whereas B and C use the V35 epoch-91 foreground and the existing frozen TRGD transfer deployment interface. The comparisons therefore have different foreground configurations: Macro Dice 90.95%→93.59% and 89.14%→92.31% are reported separately. Quantitative temporal metrics use 468,203 reference-root pixels from T2–T4 of development sequence 0353-2-B3, with background excluded from the temporal scoring domain and T1 used only as context. Both conditions in B and C retain the same 17,438 reference-root pixels missed by V35. This figure does not provide an independent temporal test or repeated-training statistical inference.'''
en_sections=[('A. Archived model comparison','''New-root precision increased from 86.71% to 94.51%, recall from 83.14% to 84.50%, Dice from 84.88% to 89.23% and IoU from 73.74% to 80.55%. The 4.34-percentage-point Dice gain was accompanied by a larger improvement in precision than in recall, consistent with fewer existing-root pixels receiving erroneous new-root labels within the reference-root domain. Existing-root Dice increased from 97.02% to 97.96%, and Macro Dice increased from 90.95% to 93.59% (+2.64 percentage points). These are pooled results for the archived comparison configuration.'''),('B. Whole-pipeline inference ablation','''With RGB inputs, V35 foreground and model weights fixed, enabling the complete TRGD process increased new-root Dice from 83.01% to 88.07% (+5.07 percentage points), existing-root Dice from 95.28% to 96.55% (+1.27) and Macro Dice from 89.14% to 92.31% (+3.17). The larger new-root gain identifies temporal state discrimination as the principal improvement. Foreground differences were zero and both controls retained 17,438 missed reference-root pixels, so the gains arose from relabelling temporal states on fixed foreground rather than detecting additional roots. This bundled ablation estimates the joint effect of the process and does not isolate the contribution of each component.'''),('C. New-root precision–recall trade-off','''Precision increased from 82.01% to 93.18% (+11.17 percentage points), whereas recall decreased from 84.02% to 83.50% (−0.53). Dice and IoU improved by 5.07 and 7.74 percentage points, respectively. Existing-root pixels erroneously classified as new roots decreased from 14,517 to 4,812, while correctly classified new-root pixels decreased slightly from 66,193 to 65,778. The output was therefore more conservative for new roots, reducing erroneous new-root labels at a small cost in detection. Because background is outside this temporal metric domain, these precision changes do not measure root–background segmentation performance.'''),('D. Spatial and temporal interpretation','''The same native 420×320-pixel window is displayed across four observation times. White root overlays establish the T1 baseline; numerous gold new-root segments are visible at T2, while blue existing-root labels occupy much of the displayed network at T3 and T4. The adjacent reference and prediction columns allow spatial correspondence of root-state assignments to be inspected at crossings, fine branches and successive time points. Additional counts on the displayed reference-root pixels show errors decreasing from 1,701 to 130 at T2 and from 135 to 58 at T4, but increasing from 512 to 693 at T3, demonstrating spatial and temporal heterogeneity. This archived qualitative example supports interpretation of A; it neither replaces whole-field statistics nor demonstrates improved upstream binary foreground detection.'''),('Scope and limitations','''The different foreground configurations in A/D and B/C prevent the 93.59% and 92.31% values from being interpreted as direct model deterioration or an additional gain. The pooled B/C improvements are not uniform across periods: the supplied per-period results show T4 new-root Dice decreasing from 75.13% to 69.46%. Conclusions are therefore restricted to pooled development-sequence performance, with a remaining limitation in late-period new-root classification. Correlated pixels within one sequence are not independent biological replicates, and no significance claim is made.''')]
cn='# 图注\n\n'+cn_caption+'\n\n'+cn_note+'\n\n# 逐图分析\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('## '+h+'\n\n'+t for h,t in cn_sections)+'\n';en='# Figure caption\n\n'+en_caption+'\n\n'+en_note+'\n\n# Panel-by-panel interpretation\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('## '+h+'\n\n'+t for h,t in en_sections)+'\n'
(P/(K+'_caption_analysis_CN.md')).write_text(cn);(P/(K+'_caption_analysis_EN.md')).write_text(en)
doc=Document();st=doc.styles['Normal'];st.font.name='Times New Roman';st.font.size=Pt(11);st.font.color.rgb=RGBColor(0,0,0);st._element.get_or_add_rPr().rFonts.set(qn('w:eastAsia'),'SimSun');st.paragraph_format.line_spacing=1.25
